data.content:
Here's the approach:

### What changed
`InvoiceCalculator` now takes an optional `TimeProvider` (defaults to `TimeProvider.System`, so existing callers are unaffected).

### In tests
Use the built-in `Microsoft.Extensions.Time.Testing.FakeTimeProvider`:

```csharp
var fake = new FakeTimeProvider(new DateTimeOffset(2026, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var calc = new InvoiceCalculator(fake);

Assert.True(calc.IsOverdue(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 12, 31, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero)));

fake.SetUtcNow(new DateTimeOffset(2024, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
Assert.False(calc.IsOverdue(new DateTimeOffset(2025, 12, 31, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero)));
```

Add the `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing` NuGet package to your test project for `FakeTimeProvider`. The library itself needs no extra packages — `TimeProvider` is in `System` since .NET 8.
